      "message": "Send an anonymous git client where a public repository went\n\nThe git door asks a stranger for a credential rather than say whether a\nrepository exists, so a clone at a public repository's former address\nwas refused where the pages and the API already redirected. The\nredirect now covers that answer too, under the same rule: only where\nthe repository is readable to whoever is asking. The first-run walk\nclones at a renamed public repository's old address to hold it there.\n\nA member of an organisation holds what the organisation holds. The\nprevious change let a member create under it and accept for it, but\nownership itself was still checked as equality with the actor, so the\nmember who had just made a repository could not read it. Ownership now\nmeans being the owner or belonging to the organisation that is, in the\none place authority is decided and the one place readability is, and a\ntest makes a person outside the organisation try both doors.\n\nAn owner with nothing public is nothing to a stranger, the way a\nprivate repository is: the owner page no longer confirms a name for\nfree. The walk makes an organisation, joins it and creates under it,\nwhich the README now describes. The documents install from\n/git/cairn/cairn, where this repository lives since its organisation\ntook it, and the README's list of what is missing drops organisations.\n\nChange-Id: Iowners0098doors\nSigned-off-by: Mandip Adhikari <92096340+mandipadk@users.noreply.github.com>",
